  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1030 PM CDT WED JUN 3 2026\n\nA relatively dry surface and mid-level ridge remains in control\nof our weather through Friday, resulting in fair-weather\nconditions and a noticeably less-muggy air mass.\n\nOver the weekend, moist onshore flow returns as the surface ridge\nrepositions. The mid-level ridge is shown to become dampened by\nshortwave troughs on its perimeter. This will promote the return\nof showers and thunderstorms to the region, continuing into a\nchunk of next week. For your weekend plans, trends favor a\ngreater coverage of activity on Sunday vs. Saturday.\n\n89^GSatterwhite",
